{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_3ektwbri5kw35wsseg3ohelkca2p6my5vq53wmujnuuzicxavhuq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All phases complete. Final state:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Phase A — artifacts** (all in `translation/`):\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — derived from `nm -D`. The C CMake build produces *three* `.so`s (`libsphincs_core.so`, `libsphincs_core_det.so`, `lib<backend>.so`), and `libsphincs_core*.so` isn't self-contained, so `scripts/build_c.sh` links one self-contained C `.so` per config from exactly the same translation units for comparison.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 42 rows, grepped mechanically from every `return -1` / `RNG_BAD_*` / `#error` / null check / range check.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 52 rows over the real branch axes: 4 backends × 2 thash × 6 secpar (48 builds), `thash(inblocks)` ∈ {0,1,2,WOTS_LEN,FORS_TREES}, message lengths at every block/rate boundary, leaf-index parity/extremes, and the `wots_sign_leaf == leaf_idx` signing branch.\n\n**Phases B/C — tests** (`translation/tests/`, ~127 KB): both `.so`s loaded via `libloading`, every call through `dlsym`, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrappers are under test. Harness params are re-derived from the C headers independently of `src/params.rs`; all output buffers carry canary tails and are compared in full.\n\n**5 real divergences found and fixed (Rust only; `c_src/` untouched):**\n1. **BLAKE `gen_message_random` wrote the wrong number of bytes** — `hash_blake.c:68` finalises straight into `R`, emitting the full 32/64-byte digest, not `SPX_N`. Caught by the canary buffers.\n2. **Missing `#[repr(C)]`** on `SpxCtx`, `LeafInfoX1`, `ForsGenLeafInfo`, `BlakeState256/512` — rustc could reorder fields under a C caller.\n3. **6 unexported symbols**: `AES256_ECB`, `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update`, `seedexpander{,_init}`, `cst`, and `DRBG_ctx` (which required replacing a `Mutex<...>` with a C-layout `static mut`).\n4. **`crypto_sign_verify` dereferenced before validating `siglen`** — `sign.c:179` returns `-1` first, so NULL `m`/`pk` are legal there.\n5. **Over-broad exports**: `shake128*`/`sha3_*` were exported although `fips202.c` only *declares* them — the symbol diff is now empty in both directions.\n\nFaithfully reproduced C quirks are documented in `VERIFICATION.md`, notably that `hash_blake.c` passes *byte* counts to `blakeX_update`, which reads them as *bit* counts — so only `mlen/8` message bytes reach the BLAKE digest.\n\n**Completion gate — 48/48 configurations:**\n\n| gate | status |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo check`/`build`, all 48 feature combos | 48/48, warning-free |\n| `nm -D` symbol diff, both directions | empty, 48/48 |\n| Rust undefined non-libc symbols | none |\n| `CONFIGS.md` 52 rows (randomized, seeded) | pass, 48/48 |\n| `ERRORS.md` 42 rows (39 tested, 3 unreachable & documented) | pass, 48/48 |\n\nTwo caveats worth flagging: a transient SIGSEGV I initially blamed on `dlopen`/`dlclose` was diagnosed by an independent audit as test-thread stack exhaustion; I applied both mitigations (load-once + `RUST_MIN_STACK`) rather than isolating the true cause. And `ERRORS.md` row 32 (`bytes_to_ull` with `inlen > 8`) asserts agreement on behaviour that is UB in C — it happens to match on this toolchain, but that row pins an observation, not a guarantee."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":364,"cache_read_input_tokens":396320,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":364,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6db5455e-f768-477c-9943-e81d8027edae","uuid":"e3eaa22b-fede-49cb-8ada-fbaf9ab14c5b","timestamp":"2026-08-29T01:01:07.441Z"}
