ypto_sign_verify` dereferenced before validating `siglen`** — `sign.c:179` returns `-1` first, so NULL `m`/`pk` are legal there.\n5. **Over-broad exports**: `shake128*`/`sha3_*` were exported although `fips202.c` only *declares* them — the symbol diff is now empty in both directions.\n\nFaithfully reproduced C quirks are documented in `VERIFICATION.md`, notably that `hash_blake.c` passes *byte* counts to `blakeX_update`, which reads them as *bit* counts — so only `mlen/8` message bytes reach the BLAKE digest.\n\n**Completion gate — 48/48 configurations:**\n\n| gate | status |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo check`/`build`, all 48 feature combos | 48/48, warning-free |\n| `nm -D` symbol diff, both directions | empty, 48/48 |\n| Rust undefined non-libc symbols | none |\n| `CONFIGS.md` 52 rows (randomized, seeded) | pass, 48/48 |\n| `ERRORS.md` 42 rows (39 tested, 3 unreachable & documented) | pass, 48/48 |\n\nTwo caveats worth flagging: a transient SIGSEGV I initially blamed on `dlopen`/`dlclose` was diagnosed by an independent audit as test-thread stack exhaustion; I applied both mitigations (load-once + `RUST_MIN_STACK`) rather than isolating the true cause. And `ERRORS.md` row 32 (`bytes_to_ull` with `inlen > 8`) asserts agreement on behaviour that is UB in C — it happens to match on this toolchain, but that row pins an observation, not a guarantee.","ttft_ms":3658,"ttft_stream_ms":3464,"time_to_request_ms":47,"type":"result","duration_ms":4799525,"uuid":"a863ced3-e530-4d13-a06a-92fbb14c397b","queued_turn_count":0}
